{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light-induced, transition-metal-free alkynylation of alkyl pinacol boronates (alkyl-Bpin) using alkynylphenylsulfones as reagents and 4CzIPN as an organic photocatalyst. The method utilizes NaOMe or NaOH as Lewis bases to form photoactive tetra-coordinated boron ate complexes, enabling the generation of alkyl radicals from primary, secondary, and tertiary alkyl-Bpin under mild conditions. Key findings include high functional group tolerance, selective monoalkynylation of diboronates, and successful application to natural product derivatives.",
